meta {
  name: update self (display name)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

patch {
  url: {{user_url}}/users/{{user_id}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "display_name": "Alice Prime"
  }
}

docs {
  Self-service profile edit: expect 200 with the updated user. Absent
  fields keep their value; an empty avatar_url string clears the
  avatar. Because logins fill the profile only at account creation,
  this edit survives every later login.

  Validation answers 400 invalid_body naming the field: a blank or
  >100-char display_name, or an avatar_url that is not http(s) or is
  over 2048 chars. Editing anyone else (or with a service/admin token)
  answers 403: profiles are self-service only.

  The direct DELETE /users/{id} endpoint deliberately has no flow
  here: deleting the row alone would orphan the account's collection
  data. The orchestrated deletion lives in bff "delete me".
}
